10-40 mg for 1-3 days 
B.     Chronic Gout – following treatment of acute gout
 Evidence Rating: [B]
yy
Allopurinol, oral, 
100 mg daily
Then
Increase by 100 mg every 2-5 weeks, adjusted if necessary for renal 
function, until the therapeutic target (Serum Uric Acid [SUA] < 300 
micromol/L) is reached (max. dose 900 mg)
Caution 22-5.
Do not start Allopurinol until 1-2 weeks after inflammation has settled to pre­
vent acute flare. But in patients already on allopurinol, it should be continued 
and the acute attack treated as usual.
Prescribe lower doses in renal or hepatic failure.'),
