240.	Chronic Osteomyelitis and Chronic Septic Arthritis
These are usually from inadequately treated acute episodes, which 
include acute osteomyelitis, acute septic arthritis, acute-on-chronic 
osteomyelitis, and acute-on-chronic septic arthritis. Some may arise from 
the onset as a chronic infection due to mycobacteria or fungi. 
The patient is usually not ill-looking unless there is an acute 
exacerbation.
