Chapter 23: Trauma And Injuries
615
244.	Tuberculosis in orthopaedics
Tuberculosis can affect all bones and joints. The spine is affected in 
50% of all cases. It affects all ages but commoner in the extremes of age. 
May co-exist with pulmonary TB in some cases and also in HIV positive 
patients.
There may be a positive history of contact with a TB infected patient.
Causes 
yy
Mycobacterium tuberculosis 
yy
Mycobacterium africanum 
yy
Mycobacterium bovis
