245.	Rickets and Osteomalacia
Rickets is caused by failure of osteoid to calcify in a growing person 
resulting in softening and weakening of bones, due to extreme or 
prolonged vitamin-D deficiency.
Osteomalacia is essentially its equivalent in the skeletally mature.
Causes 
yy
Vitamin-D deficiency due to:
yy
Reduced intake (nutritional is the commonest)
yy
Malabsorption 
yy
Reduced sunlight 
yy
Vitamin-D resistance
yy
Vitamin-D dependence
