248.	Sickle-cell Vaso-occlusive Crisis
This is a painful complication of sickle-cell disease, induced by 
obstruction of small blood vessels by crystallized sickle cells leading 
to ischaemic injury to several organs, including bone. The bone pain is 
usually difficult to distinguish from acute osteomyelitis. 
Causes 
