251.	Burns 
A burn is basically destruction of the skin. In certain situations 
deeper tissues such as subcutaneous tissue, muscle and bone may be 
involved. The burn may be superficial or deep depending on the extent of 
the injury. This condition, which can have devastating effects on affected 
people, can be prevented most of the time. It affects young and fit people 
in most cases and they must be managed properly so that they can return 
to their normal life.
Causes 
yy
Dry heat (fire)
yy
Wet heat (scalds) from hot liquids, steam, soups etc.
yy
Electrical (low or high voltage)
yy
Chemical (acids and alkalis)
Symptoms
yy
Pain (very severe in superficial type and less in deeper burns)
yy
Swelling 
yy
Difficulty in breathing 
yy
Blisters 
 

