itis yy Blood - Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation yy Metabolic - Hyperglycemia, Hypoglycemia yy Immune system - Immune depression','Refer to a tertiary centre when symptoms of rabies set in. 254. Shock Shock is a clinical state of cellular dysfunction as a result of decreased circulating blood volume leading to reduction in delivery of oxygen and other nutrients to vital organs which if prolonged leads to irreversible multiple organ failure. Causes yy Hypovolemia e.g. haemorrhage, vomiting, diarrhoea, acute intestinal obstruction yy Cardiogenic e.g. myocardial infarction, Massive pulmonary embolus yy Obstructive e.g. Pericardial tamponade, tension pneumothorax yy Severe sepsis Symptoms yy Thirst yy Feeling faint yy Palpitations yy Sweating yy Restlessness','— Shock —
