255.	Acute Allergic Reaction (Anaphylaxis) 
An acute allergic reaction or anaphylaxis is a life-threatening 
but rapidly reversible condition if treated promptly. Anaphylaxis can 
develop within minutes of injection or ingestion of medicines or contact 
with allergen. Persons who are aware of the risk of anaphylaxis are to 
be informed of avoidance measures, and may be taught the use of an 
epinephrine (adrenaline) pen.   
